-- title:
--   Hecke–Galois datum at cube-free level, p=3
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime with $p \neq 2$ and $p = 3$, and let $W$ be a Weierstrass curve over $\mathbb{Z}$ with $\Delta_W \neq 0$ which is a semistable model, i.e. no prime $q$ dividing $\Delta_W$ divides $c_4(W)$, and whose mod $p$ representation is irreducible in the sense that the $p$-torsion of $W$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is nontrivial and its only Galois-stable $\mathbb{Z}/p$-submodules are $0$ and the whole module. Let $M \neq 0$ satisfy: if $p^2 \mid M$, then for every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a nonunit of $A$, the only $p$-torsion point of $W$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ fixed by all elements of the inertia subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ is $0$; and no prime $q \neq p$ has $q^3 \mid M$. Assume $W$ is residually modular of level $M$: there are a normalised eigenform $f$ of weight $2$ on $\Gamma_0(M)$ and a maximal ideal $\mathfrak{m}$ of the integral closure of $\mathbb{Z}$ in $\mathbb{C}$ with $p \in \mathfrak{m}$ such that for every prime $\ell$ with $\ell \nmid \Delta_W$, $\ell \nmid M$, $\ell \neq p$ the $\ell$-th $q$-coefficient of $f$ is an algebraic integer congruent mod $\mathfrak{m}$ to $a_\ell(W)$, the trace of Frobenius of the reduction of $W$ mod $\ell$. Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a complete discrete valuation ring of characteristic zero with finite residue field and $p$ in its maximal ideal. Then there are a finite set $S$ of primes with $p \in S$ containing every prime dividing $\Delta_W$, and a nonzero level $N$, such that every prime dividing $N$ lies in $S$; $q^2 \mid N$ and $q^3 \nmid N$ for every $q \in S$ with $q \neq p$; if $p \mid \Delta_W$ or $p \nmid a_p(W)$ then $p \mid N$ and $p^2 \nmid N$, while if $p \nmid \Delta_W$ and $p \mid a_p(W)$ then $p \nmid N$; the $\mathbb{C}$-span of the cusp forms in $S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ with integral $q$-expansion coefficients is all of $S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$; and, writing $\mathbb{T}$ for the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}} S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ ($\ell$ prime, $\ell \nmid N$, $\ell \notin S$) and $U_q$ ($q$ prime, $q \mid N$, $q \notin S$), there is a ring homomorphism $\theta : \mathbb{T} \to \mathcal{O}/\mathfrak{m}_{\mathcal{O}}$ with $\theta(T_\ell)$ the residue of $a_\ell(W)$ for all primes $\ell \nmid N$ outside $S$, together with a complete noetherian local $\mathcal{O}$-algebra $T$, local over $\mathcal{O}$ and finite and free as an $\mathcal{O}$-module, admitting a [`CuspForm.HeckeGaloisRepDatum`](def/CuspForm_HeckeGaloisRepDatum.html#L8) for $(N, S, \mathcal{O}, \theta)$: a ring homomorphism $\pi : \mathbb{T} \to T$ reducing to $\theta$, with $\mathcal{O}[\operatorname{im}\pi] = T$, through which every $\mathcal{O}$-valued character of $\mathbb{T}$ reducing to $\theta$ factors by an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra map, with surjective residual structure map, and an adic Galois representation $\rho$ over $T$ with absolutely irreducible residual representation and $\operatorname{charpoly}(\rho(\sigma)) = X^2 - \pi(T_\ell)X + \ell$ for every Frobenius element $\sigma$ at a place above any prime $\ell \nmid N$ outside $S$.
--
--   This is the input-normalising step of the Taylor–Wiles patching construction: starting from residual modularity at an arbitrary cube-free-away-from-$p$ level, it produces a Taylor–Wiles level $N$ of the prescribed shape (square but not cube at the auxiliary primes, $p$-part exactly $p$ in the ordinary case and trivial in the flat case) together with the associated Hecke algebra character and Hecke–Galois representation datum. It is used by the corresponding statement that adjoins a finite extension of $\mathcal{O}$ and a patching datum.
